">🤖 AI can help adapt reading materials for different reading levels while keeping key ideas intact. </div> </details>

<div style="float:right; width:260px; margin:0 0 12px 20px;">
  <img 
    src="https://images.code.org/af7b2bee0c86b226155429d71a79b6ff-cc0fad62-a625-4b97-b54f-a101867d33a1.png"
    alt="Cartoon ecosystem illustration"
    style="width:100%; border-radius:10px; border:1px solid #D9DDE3;"
  >
</div>

Knowing she's needed at home soon, she makes one final edit, prints the passages, and calls it a night.

The next day, students complete an exit ticket before leaving class. As Ms. Garcia reviews their responses after school, she notices a pattern. Most students can identify organisms in a food web, but many struggle to explain what happens when one population changes. The misunderstanding is clear, but the cause is not.

Did students misunderstand the concept itself? Were the examples she used ineffective? Was the reading passage still too difficult? She isn't sure.

<details style="display:inline;"> <summary style="
cursor:pointer;
display:inline;
font-size:15px;
font-weight:400;
line-height:1.5;
color:#555;
"> <div style="
margin:8px 0 8px 24px;
padding-left:12px;
border-left:3px solid #DDD6F3;
color:#666;
"> <span style="font-size:0.7em;">▶ </span><i>"I know students have a misconception, but I'm not sure why they're getting stuck or what I should do differently tomorrow."</i> </summary>
  
<div style="
margin-top:10px;
margin-left:20px;
margin-bottom:20px;
background:#F7F8FA;
border:1px solid #D9DDE3;
border-radius:10px;
padding:12px 14px;
font-size:15px;
line-height:1.5;
color:#555;
">🤖 AI can help identify possible misconceptions and suggest ways to reteach a concept. </div> </details>

Needing to address the issue quickly, Ms. Garcia decides to begin the next class by reteaching the key concept. She knows there may be more targeted ways to respond, but she doesn't have enough information to confidently choose the best next step.

---

> **💬 Quick Reflection:** What resonates with you in this story? Are there any parts of your teaching practice which you'd like to improve using AI integration?
